Date: Fri, 30 Oct 2026 23:52:54 +0100
Subject: [PATCH] Tools: Dump Memory After SpotPass Reads (Build 139)

Nintendogs + Cats reads a downloaded SpotPass neighbour at no fixed
moment (37 s, 95 s and 213 s after start in the 30 Oct tests) and checks
and stores it right after, so a hand-timed Tools > Dump Process Memory
came too early or too late.

Tools > Dump Memory After SpotPass Reads (a tick, off at every start):
while it is on, the kernel watches a game's ReadNsData (boss:U
0x00280102) and, when the SpotPass module answers it with success,
tells the frontend (Kernel::SetSpotPassReadCallback). 3 seconds after
the last such read the game's memory is dumped like Dump Process Memory,
as dump/memory/<title id>-<date-time>-after-nsdata-<NsData ID>.bin and
.txt, without dialogs (a status bar message and a Frontend Info log
line instead). Several reads in a row give one dump.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
Claude-Session: https://claude.ai/code/session_01FYz3krf43qKGY6aS2Z5snz
